    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="0850" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/1715</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Mexican Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Téllez</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-27">April 27, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note dated April 16, 1931, and its enclosures, concerning an
                    action <pb facs="0851" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/> brought in the Supreme Court of
                    the State of New York in and for the County of New York against Thomas W. Lamont
                    and others, and the United Mexican States.</p>
                <p>I have returned the documents enclosed with your note to the Governor of New York
                    with a statement that your Government does not consent to be sued and that
                    neither you nor the Consul General of Mexico have any right to accept service on
                    behalf of your Government.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
